{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "02757",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 0.71,
      "end_seconds": 8.59,
      "duration_seconds": 7.88,
      "text": "Doctor, the patient's with us now. I did the usual checks at the front, so just say when you want them."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 9.22,
      "end_seconds": 12.2,
      "duration_seconds": 2.98,
      "text": "Thank you. Right, hello, what's the problem?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 18.06,
      "end_seconds": 30.05,
      "duration_seconds": 11.99,
      "text": "So the thing is, I've got a dull ache on one side of the chest. My sister suggested writing things down, but I forgot."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 32.04,
      "end_seconds": 34.84,
      "duration_seconds": 2.8,
      "text": "Has this been going on for long?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 35.45,
      "end_seconds": 46.88,
      "duration_seconds": 11.43,
      "text": "It's been three days, I'm fairly sure. Sorry, I know I'm rambling a bit. I've also had a dry cough, for two days."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 47.42,
      "end_seconds": 50.76,
      "duration_seconds": 3.34,
      "text": "Is there any regular medication you use?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 51.94,
      "end_seconds": 56.49,
      "duration_seconds": 4.55,
      "text": "Erm, you know, no, nothing at the moment."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 57.76,
      "end_seconds": 63.66,
      "duration_seconds": 5.9,
      "text": "Any medical conditions, anything you've been treated for? Take your time, there's no rush."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 64.42,
      "end_seconds": 67.22,
      "duration_seconds": 2.8,
      "text": "No, I've always been fairly healthy."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 77.8,
      "end_seconds": 81.2,
      "duration_seconds": 3.4,
      "text": "So, do you follow any particular diet?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 83.29,
      "end_seconds": 87.07,
      "duration_seconds": 3.78,
      "text": "I'm vegetarian and have been for years."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 87.81,
      "end_seconds": 90.27,
      "duration_seconds": 2.46,
      "text": "Do you get out much?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 91.67,
      "end_seconds": 95.63,
      "duration_seconds": 3.96,
      "text": "Not much, I mostly stay in these days."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 114.28,
      "end_seconds": 118.84,
      "duration_seconds": 4.56,
      "text": "What about your parents, brothers or sisters, any conditions?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 119.48,
      "end_seconds": 122.97,
      "duration_seconds": 3.49,
      "text": "Okay, so my cousin has psoriasis."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 124.03,
      "end_seconds": 126.72,
      "duration_seconds": 2.69,
      "text": "Before we go further, any allergies?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 127.94,
      "end_seconds": 130.97,
      "duration_seconds": 3.03,
      "text": "Yes, diclofenac, it gives me wheezing."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 140.39,
      "end_seconds": 143.23,
      "duration_seconds": 2.84,
      "text": "Did you ever have any procedures done?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 144.29,
      "end_seconds": 151.22,
      "duration_seconds": 6.93,
      "text": "Yes, I had a wisdom tooth extraction under sedation, five years ago."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 155.1,
      "end_seconds": 161.67,
      "duration_seconds": 6.57,
      "text": "Let me check a few things. Any coughing up blood, night sweats or fever?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 163.48,
      "end_seconds": 166.0,
      "duration_seconds": 2.52,
      "text": "No, none that I've noticed."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 166.28,
      "end_seconds": 169.32,
      "duration_seconds": 3.04,
      "text": "Mm-hmm. Has your skin been okay?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 171.38,
      "end_seconds": 172.28,
      "duration_seconds": 0.9,
      "text": "No rashes."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 175.59,
      "end_seconds": 185.96,
      "duration_seconds": 10.37,
      "text": "Here are the numbers, doctor. SpO2 94 percent on room air, pulse 90, respiratory rate 26, temperature is 36.9 degrees, pressure 123 over 80."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 188.06,
      "end_seconds": 188.98,
      "duration_seconds": 0.92,
      "text": "Okay, noted."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 190.56,
      "end_seconds": 194.57,
      "duration_seconds": 4.01,
      "text": "Let me look at the area, I'll be gentle."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 209.98,
      "end_seconds": 211.09,
      "duration_seconds": 1.11,
      "text": "Okay, doctor."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 212.07,
      "end_seconds": 213.47,
      "duration_seconds": 1.4,
      "text": "Nearly finished here."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 227.47,
      "end_seconds": 233.72,
      "duration_seconds": 6.25,
      "text": "There is dullness to percussion and reduced breath sounds at the right base."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 237.55,
      "end_seconds": 246.81,
      "duration_seconds": 9.26,
      "text": "All finished, thank you. Okay, thinking it through, the most likely explanation is a pleural effusion needing a cause."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 248.6,
      "end_seconds": 251.69,
      "duration_seconds": 3.09,
      "text": "Do you think it's something serious?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 255.03,
      "end_seconds": 290.91,
      "duration_seconds": 35.88,
      "text": "I understand the worry. At the moment I'd say it's a pleural effusion needing a cause, and we'll know more once the a CT scan of the chest is back. I'm going to order a CT scan of the chest, for pleural effusion. The result will help us decide whether anything more is needed. I am arranging an urgent chest clinic review. The chest clinic would be the right next step, I'll refer you."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 292.25,
      "end_seconds": 294.62,
      "duration_seconds": 2.37,
      "text": "Sure, where do I go?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 296.25,
      "end_seconds": 309.22,
      "duration_seconds": 12.97,
      "text": "Let's hold off on a pleural fluid sample for now, and if there's no change in a month we can revisit it. Anything else on your mind before you go?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 310.84,
      "end_seconds": 314.53,
      "duration_seconds": 3.69,
      "text": "Right, I'll do that. Thank you, doctor."
    }
  ]
}